  "Number": 21,
  "Question": "The volume of a rectangular solid each of whose side, front, and bottom faces are \\(12\\) square inches, \\(8\\) square inches, and \\(6\\) square inches respectively is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(576\\) cubic inches",
    "B": "\\(24\\) cubic inches",
    "C": "\\(9\\) cubic inches",
    "D": "\\(104\\) cubic inches",
    "E": "None of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Let \\(a,b,c>0\\) be the solid's three perpendicular edge lengths, measured in inches. Its side, front, and bottom areas are \\(ab\\), \\(ac\\), and \\(bc\\), in some order.\n\nMultiplying these areas uses each edge length twice. Thus, if \\(V=abc\\) is the numerical volume in cubic inches,\n\\[\nV^2=(ab)(ac)(bc)=12\\cdot8\\cdot6=576.\n\\]\nSince the volume is positive, \\(V=\\sqrt{576}=24\\). The volume is \\(\\boxed{24\\text{ cubic inches}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
